For explosions we considered three regimes: 
 \begin{align}
\text{Regime 1:}\quad& d\simeq c_0 t\\
\text{Regime 2:}\quad& d\simeq K t^\frac{2}{5}\\
\text{Regime 3:}\quad& d\simeq c_s t
\end{align}
These three regimes lead to two points of intersection: 
\begin{align}
\text{Regime 1} \cap \text{Regime 2} \quad \rightarrow  t_0\simeq \Big(\frac{K}{c_0} \Big)^\frac{5}{3} \quad \& \quad d_0\simeq \frac{K^\frac{5}{3}}{c_0^\frac{2}{3}}\label{todo} \\
\text{Regime 2} \cap \text{Regime 3} \quad \rightarrow  t_*\simeq \Big(\frac{K}{c_s} \Big)^\frac{5}{3} \quad \& \quad d_*\simeq \frac{K^\frac{5}{3}}{c_s^\frac{2}{3}}\label{txdx}
\end{align}

