\section{Preliminaries}

\subsection{Problem Description}
% 我们将超图 $\mathcal{G}$ 定义为一个二元组 $(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$, 其中 $\mathcal{V} = \{v_1, v_2, \dots, v_m\}$ 表示节点集合, $\mathcal{E} = \{e_1, e_2, \dots, e_n\}$ 表示超边集合 \cite{berge1989, bretto2013hypergraphs}. 节点特征由矩阵 $\mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times d}$ 表示, 其中每一行向量 $\mathbf{x}_i \in \mathbb{R}^d$ 对应于节点 $v_i$ 自身所固有的 $d$ 维特征. 与简单图中边仅能连接两个节点不同, 超图中的超边 $e_j \subseteq \mathcal{E}$ 是节点集的任意非空子集, 能够表示多个节点之间的高阶交互关系. 超图的结构信息可通过关联矩阵 $\mathbf{H} \in \{0, 1\}^{m \times n}$ 表示, 其中矩阵元素 $H_{ij}$ 满足: 当且仅当 $v_i \in e_j$ 时, $H_{ij} = 1$; 否则 $H_{ij} = 0$. 基于关联矩阵 $\mathbf{H}$, 我们可以定义超图的基本拓扑属性: 节点 $v_i \in \mathcal{V}$ 的度 $d_i$ 表示包含该节点的超边数量, 其计算公式为 $d_{i} = \sum_{j=1}^{n} H_{ij}$; 相应地, 超边 $e_j \in \mathcal{E}$ 的势$c_j$表示该超边包含的节点数量, 其计算公式为 $c_{j} = \sum_{i=1}^{m} H_{ij}$. 
We formally define a hypergraph $\mathcal{G}$ as a binary tuple $(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$, where $\mathcal{V} = \{v_1, v_2, \dots, v_m\}$ denotes the node set and $\mathcal{E} = \{e_1, e_2, \dots, e_n\}$ represents the hyperedge set \cite{berge1984, bretto2013hypergraphs}. Node features are encoded in a matrix $\mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times d}$, where each row vector $\mathbf{x}_i \in \mathbb{R}^d$ corresponds to the intrinsic $d$-dimensional features of node $v_i$. Unlike simple graphs where a link connects only two nodes, a hyperedge $e_j \subseteq \mathcal{V}$ can be an arbitrary non-empty subset of nodes, enabling the representation of higher-order interactions among multiple entities. The structural information of the hypergraph is captured by an incidence matrix $\mathbf{H} \in \{0, 1\}^{m \times n}$, where the element $h_{ij}$ is set to $1$ if and only if $v_i \in e_j$; conversely, if $v_i$ does not belong to $e_j$, then $h_{ij}$ is set to $0$. The degree $d_i$ of node $v_i \in \mathcal{V}$, representing the number of hyperedges containing it, is $d_{i} = \sum_{j=1}^{n} h_{ij}$. Correspondingly, the order $c_j$ of hyperedge $e_j \in \mathcal{E}$, indicating the number of nodes it contains, is $c_{j} = \sum_{i=1}^{m} h_{ij}$.


% 超边预测是基于已经观察到的超边集合$\mathcal{E}$和节点特征$\mathbf{X}$（一般而言，前者是必须的，后者或有或无）去预测存在但还未被观察到的超边或者未来将会出现的超边。记目标超边集合（i.e., 还未被观察到的超边或者未来将会出现的超边）为 $\mathcal{E}'$，满足$\mathcal{E}' \cap \mathcal{E} = \emptyset$，超边预测可以被形式化为一个二分类问题：给定$\mathcal{G}(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$ 及 $\mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times d}$，对于任意候选超边 $e\notin \mathcal{E}$, 目标是预测 $e$ 是否属于 $\mathcal{E}'$. 
Hyperedge prediction aims to infer unobserved or future hyperedges based on the observed hyperedge set $\mathcal{E}$ and node features $\mathbf{X}$ (generally speaking, the former is essential, while the latter may or may not be present). Let the target hyperedge set (\textit{i.e.}, unobserved or future hyperedges) be $\mathcal{E}'$ such that $\mathcal{E}' \cap \mathcal{E} = \emptyset$. This task can be formalized as a binary classification problem: Given a hypergraph $\mathcal{G}(\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$ and node features $\mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times d}$, for any candidate hyperedge $e \notin \mathcal{E}$, the objective is to predict whether $e$ belongs to $\mathcal{E}'$. 


\subsection{Pipeline of Hyperedge Prediction}

\begin{figure}[ht]
	\centering
	\includegraphics[width=0.95\linewidth]{figures/HyperEdgeLinkPrediction_Pipeline.pdf}
	\caption{\textbf{The flowchart of a learning-based hyperedge prediction framework}. This framework consists of four sequential stages: (1) Node Embedding: Using hypergraph neural networks to embed nodes; (2) Hyperedge Embedding: Generating hyperedge embeddings through neighborhood aggregation; (3) Prediction: Classifying hyperedge embeddings to predict the existence of hyperedges; and (4) Loss Calculation and Model Update: Computing the loss between predicted values and true labels, and updating model parameters accordingly.}
	\label{fig:HELP_Pipeline}
\end{figure}

% 基于嵌入的超边预测框架主要由三个核心组件构成\cite{yadati2020nhp,hwang2022ahp,li2023interpretable}: 编码器 (encoder), 聚合器 (aggregator)和分类器 (classifier), 其整体架构如图\ref{fig:HELP_Pipeline}所示. 编码器的任务是将超图中的节点嵌入到高维的向量空间中, 这些嵌入向量不仅能够反映出节点自身属性之间的相似性, 同时也能反映节点在网络当中的结构相似性, 为后续的超边预测提供了基础. 聚合器的作用是将任意一条候选超边所包含所有节点的嵌入向量整合为该超边对应的嵌入向量. 最后, 分类器根据聚合器生成的候选超边的嵌入向量进行分类, 判断该超边是否属于目标超边集合 $\mathcal{E}'$. 分类器的输出是一个概率值, 表示该候选超边属于$\mathcal{E}'$的概率. 接下来, 我们将对每个组件的实现细节进行更加详细的介绍. 
The embedding-based hyperedge prediction framework comprises three core components \cite{yadati2020nhp,hwang2022ahp,li2023interpretable}: An encoder, an aggregator, and a classifier. The overall architecture is illustrated in Figure \ref{fig:HELP_Pipeline}. The encoder maps nodes into a high-dimensional vector space. These embeddings capture both \textbf{attribute similarity} (reflecting intrinsic node properties) and \textbf{structural similarity} (reflecting topological closeness), forming the foundation for subsequent hyperedge prediction. The aggregator integrates the embeddings of all nodes involved in a candidate hyperedge to generate a unified hyperedge embedding. Finally, based on the aggregated embedding, the classifier achieves a likelihood score that determines whether the candidate hyperedge belongs to the target set $\mathcal{E}'$. Next, we elaborate on the implementation details of each component.

% 编码器旨在捕捉节点之间的相似性, 并基于此将超图中的节点表示为高维嵌入向量. 节点的相似性可以分为两类: 属性相似性和结构相似性. 属性相似性取决于节点固有的属性特征, 例如社交网络中个人的职业和兴趣爱好，其相关信息包含在节点的特征矩阵$\mathbf{X}$中. 结构相似性取决于节点在网络拓扑结构中所扮演的角色，其相关信息包含在关联矩阵$\mathbf{H}$中. 节点编码器的输出为节点的嵌入向量. 编码器的形式化定义如下
% \begin{equation}
% 	\mathbf{V} = \operatorname{Encoder}(\mathbf{H}, \mathbf{X})
% \end{equation}
% 其中$\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times h}$为所有节点的嵌入向量构成的表示矩阵，$h$为嵌入向量的维度. Encoder有多种选择，可以可以根据先验知识,采用手动构造的方法，例如SEHP\cite{li2023interpretable}, 也可以采用超图神经网络从数据当中自动学习, 例如HGNN\cite{feng2019hypergraph}, HGNNP\cite{gao2023hgnn+}, HNHN\cite{dong2020hnhn}, 或NHP\cite{yadati2020nhp}.
The encoder aims to capture the similarity between nodes and represent nodes as high-dimensional embedding vectors. Node similarity can be categorized into two types: Attribute similarity and structural similarity. Attribute similarity depends on the intrinsic attributes of nodes, such as occupation and interests of an individual in a social network, which are contained in the node feature matrix $\mathbf{X}$. Structural similarity depends on the roles that nodes play within the network topology, which is captured by the incidence matrix $\mathbf{H}$. The output of the node encoder is the embedding vectors of all nodes. Formally, the encoder can be defined as:
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf{V} = \operatorname{Encoder}(\mathbf{H}, \mathbf{X}),
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times h}$ is the representation matrix of all node, and $h$ is the dimensionality of the embedding vectors. There are multiple choices for the encoder, it can be manually constructed based on prior knowledge, such as SEHP \cite{li2023interpretable}, or it can automatically learn from data using hypergraph neural networks, such as HGNN \cite{feng2019hypergraph}, HGNNP \cite{gao2023hgnn+}, HNHN \cite{dong2020hnhn} and NHP \cite{yadati2020nhp}.


% 对于任意候选超边$e_q=\{ v_{q_1}, v_{q_2}, \dots, v_{q_{c_q}} \}$，聚合器的目标是以这$c_q$个$d$维嵌入向量为输入，输出一个$d$维向量，作为$e_q$的嵌入向量。聚合器的形式化定义如下
% \begin{equation}
% 	\mathbf{e}_q = \operatorname{Aggregator}(\mathcal{V}_q)
% \end{equation}
% 其中$\mathcal{V}_{q} = \left\{ \mathbf{v}_{q_1}, \dots, \mathbf{v}_{q_2}, \dots, \mathbf{v}_{q_{c_q}} \right\}$是通过编码器得到的$e_q$所含节点的嵌入向量, $\mathbf{e}_q \in \mathbb{R}^{h}$是超边$e_q$的嵌入向量. 常用的节点聚合函数的包括 Sum（对节点的嵌入向量在每一个维度分别求和）, Mean（对节点的嵌入向量在每一个维度分别求平均）和MaxMin（对节点的嵌入向量在每一个维度求最大值减去最小值）\cite{yadati2020nhp}.
For any candidate hyperedge $e_q=\{ v_{q_1}, v_{q_2}, \dots, v_{q_{c_q}} \}$, the goal of the aggregator is to take these $c_q$ $d$-dimensional embedding vectors as input and output a single $d$-dimensional vector as the embedding vector for $e_q$. Formally, the aggregator can be defined by:
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{e}_q = \operatorname{Aggregator}(\mathcal{V}_q),
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{V}_{q} = \left\{ \mathbf{v}_{q_1}, \dots, \mathbf{v}_{q_2}, \dots, \mathbf{v}_{q_{c_q}} \right\}$ represents the embeddings of the nodes in $e_q$, and $\mathbf{e}_q \in \mathbb{R}^{h}$ is the embedding vector for the hyperedge $e_q$. Common node aggregation functions include:  \textbf{Sum} (summing the embedding vectors of the nodes along each dimension), \textbf{Mean} (averaging the embedding vectors of the nodes along each dimension), and \textbf{MaxMin} (computing the difference between the maximum and minimum values of the embedding vectors along each dimension) \cite{yadati2020nhp}.


% 分类器的核心任务是利用候选超边的嵌入向量来预测其是否属于目标集合$\mathcal{E}'$，其形式化定义如下 
% \begin{equation}
% 	p_q = \operatorname{Classifier}(\mathbf{e}_q)
% \end{equation}
% 其中$p_q$为候选超边属于$\mathcal{E}'$的概率. 在实际应用中, 分类器通常采用前馈神经网络来实现 \cite{hornik1989multilayer}.
The core task of the classifier is to use the embedding vector of a candidate hyperedge to predict whether it belongs to the target set $\mathcal{E}'$. Usually, The classifier can be defined as:
\begin{equation}
    p_q = \operatorname{Classifier}(\mathbf{e}_q),
\end{equation}
where $p_q$ is the likelihood that the candidate hyperedge belongs to $\mathcal{E}'$. In practice, the classifier is typically implemented using a feedforward neural network \cite{hornik1989multilayer}.


\section{Methods}
% 本文提出了一种名为 HNS 的负采样方法, 其核心思想是在高维嵌入空间中, 将正样本信息注入到负样本当中, 从而生成更加难以分类的负样本。具体分为三个主要步骤: 首先, 利用超图神经网络将超边映射为稠密的嵌入向量, 以捕获高阶拓扑结构和节点属性信息; 其次, 采用基于正样本混合的嵌入扰动策略, 将正样本的嵌入特征注入到简单负样本的嵌入向量中, 从而在嵌入空间中生成一个区分难度更高的负样本; 最后, 将生成的负样本与真实正样本共同用于训练超边预测模型，以提升模型的预测精度。
This paper proposes a negative sampling method named \textbf{HNS} (hyperedge negative sampling). The core idea of HNS is to inject positive sample information into negative samples in the high-dimensional embedding space, thereby generating more challenging negative samples. Specifically, the method consists of three main steps: Firstly, hypergraph neural networks are utilized to map hyperedges into dense embedding vectors, capturing high-order topological structures and node attribute information. Secondly, an embedding perturbation strategy is employed, which injects the embedding features of positive samples into the embedding vectors of simple negative samples, thus creating more difficult-to-discriminate negative samples in the embedding space. Finally, the generated negative samples are used to train the hyperedge prediction model, thereby improving the model's prediction accuracy.


\subsection{Hyperedge Representation}
% 超边表征旨在将超边映射到高维嵌入空间, 在该空间中, 节点之间的相似性通过其向量间的距离来度量: 属性或结构上相似的节点被映射到彼此接近的位置, 而属性上不相关且结构差异较大的节点则被映射到彼此远离的位置. 这种嵌入方式将超边从复杂且往往是离散化的非欧空间映射到连续的实数空间, 使得超边之间的相似性可以通过直接计算距离进行量化, 从而为后续负样本的生成奠定了基础. 若选用HGNN编码器，则超图神经网络的编码过程可以形式化地表示为: 
% \begin{equation}
% \mathbf{V} = \operatorname{HGNN}(\mathbf{H}, \mathbf{X}; \mathbf{\Theta})
% \end{equation}
% 其中$\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times h}$是超图当中所有节点的嵌入向量所组成的嵌入矩阵, $\Theta$是超图神经网络的可学习参数. 值得强调的是, HNS方法是即插即用的，对超图编码器没有特殊要求, 因此任何能够生成节点嵌入的超图神经网络都可以与 HNS 结合使用.
Hyperedge representation aims to map hyperedges into a high-dimensional embedding space, where the similarity between nodes is measured by the distance between their vectors: Nodes that are similar in terms of attributes or structure are mapped close to each other, while dissimilar nodes are mapped far apart. This embedding approach transforms hyperedges from a complex and often discrete non-Euclidean space into a continuous Euclidean space, allowing the similarity between hyperedges to be quantified by directly computing distances. This provides a foundation for generating negative samples in subsequent steps. For example, if an HGNN encoder is chosen, the encoding process is defined as:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{V} = \operatorname{HGNN}(\mathbf{H}, \mathbf{X}; \mathbf{\Theta}),
\end{equation}
where $\Theta$ represents the learnable parameters of HGNN. It is worth emphasizing that HNS is plug-and-play and does not impose specific requirements on the hypergraph encoder. Therefore, any hypergraph neural network capable of generating node embeddings can be combined with HNS.


% 与普通的图神经网络类似, 超图神经网络的基本思想也是通过结合自身与邻居节点的信息来迭代更新嵌入向量，其数学框架如下。初始令$\mathbf{V}^{0} = \mathbf{X}$, 对于第$\kappa$层, $\kappa = 1, 2, \dots, K$有:
% \begin{align}
% 	\mathbf{a}^{\kappa}_{v} &= \operatorname{AGGERATOR}^{\kappa}\left\{ \mathbf{V}^{\kappa-1}_{u}: u \in N(v) \right\} \\
% 	\mathbf{V}^{\kappa}_{v} &= \operatorname{COMBINE}^{\kappa} \left\{ \mathbf{V}^{\kappa-1}_v, \mathbf{a}^{\kappa}_{v} \right\}
% \end{align}
% 其中, $\operatorname{AGGERATE}$函数的功能是从每个节点的邻居节点处汇总信息, $\operatorname{COMBINE}$函数的功能是通过结合来自邻居节点的聚合信息和当前节点的嵌入向量来更新当前节点的嵌入向量, $N(v)$是节点$v$的邻居节点集合, 最后一层的节点嵌入向量$\mathbf{V}^{K}$ 可以看作最终输出的节点嵌入.
Similar to ordinary graph neural networks, the fundamental idea of hypergraph neural networks is also to iteratively update embedding vectors by combining information from a node itself and its neighboring nodes. The mathematical framework is as follows: Initially, let $\mathbf{V}^{0} = \mathbf{X}$. For the $\kappa$-th layer, where $\kappa = 1, 2, \dots, K$, we have:
\begin{align}
	\mathbf{a}^{\kappa}_{v} &= \operatorname{AGGERATOR}^{\kappa}\left\{ \mathbf{V}^{\kappa-1}_{u}: u \in N(v) \right\}, \\
	\mathbf{V}^{\kappa}_{v} &= \operatorname{COMBINE}^{\kappa} \left\{ \mathbf{V}^{\kappa-1}_v, \mathbf{a}^{\kappa}_{v} \right\},
\end{align}
where the function $\operatorname{AGGERATE}$ aggregates information from the neighboring nodes of each node, and the function $\operatorname{COMBINE}$ updates the current node's embedding by combining the aggregated information from neighboring nodes with the current node's embedding. $N(v)$ is the set of neighboring nodes of node $v$. The final node embeddings $\mathbf{V}^{K}$ from the last layer can be considered the ultimate output of node embeddings.


% 在生成节点嵌入后, 可以通过聚合的方式构造任意候选超边的表示. 给定一条候选超边 $e_q = \{ v_{q_1}, v_{q_2}, \dots, v_{q_{c_q}} \}$, 可以通过聚合函数对这些节点的嵌入向量进行汇总, 生成超边$e_q$的嵌入向量. 以前的研究表明，效果较好的聚合函数是 MaxMin 函数\cite{yadati2020nhp}, 因此我们选用该函数（HNS或其他作为对比分析的负抽样方法对于聚合函数的选择没有特别的要求），具体如下：
% \begin{align}
% 	\mathbf{\text{Max}} &= \left( \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}} \mathbf{v}_i^{(1)}, \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(2)}, \dots, \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(h)} \right) \\
% 	\mathbf{\text{Min}} &= \left( \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}} \mathbf{v}_i^{(1)}, \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(2)}, \dots, \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(h)} \right) \\
% 	\mathbf{\text{MaxMin}} &= \mathbf{\text{Max}} - \mathbf{\text{Min}}
% \end{align}
% 候选超边的嵌入向量即为$\mathbf{e}_q=\operatorname{MaxMin}$.
After generating node embeddings, we can construct the representation of any candidate hyperedge through aggregation. Given a candidate hyperedge $e_q = \{ v_{q_1}, v_{q_2}, \dots, v_{q_{c_q}} \}$, we can aggregate the embeddings of these nodes to generate the embedding vector for hyperedge $e_q$. Previous study has shown that the \textit{MaxMin} function is effective for this purpose \cite{yadati2020nhp}, so we adopt this function (note that HNS or other negative sampling methods do not impose specific requirements on the choice of aggregation functions). The process is as follows:
\begin{align}
	\mathbf{\text{Max}} &= \left( \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}} \mathbf{v}_i^{(1)}, \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(2)}, \dots, \max_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(h)} \right), \\
	\mathbf{\text{Min}} &= \left( \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}} \mathbf{v}_i^{(1)}, \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(2)}, \dots, \min_{i=q_1, q_2, \dots, q_{c_q}}\mathbf{v}_i^{(h)} \right), \\
	\mathbf{\text{MaxMin}} &= \mathbf{\text{Max}} - \mathbf{\text{Min}}.
\end{align}
The embedding vector of the candidate hyperedge is then given by $\mathbf{e}_q=\operatorname{MaxMin}$.



\subsection{Negative Sample Generation}

\begin{figure}[ht]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.7\linewidth]{figures/inject.pdf}
    \caption{\textbf{Illustration of how to generate negative samples by HNS}. This framework operates through three sequential stages: (1) Weight Calculation: Compute the normalized weights between positive and negative sample embeddings, which will be further utilized to determine the contribution of each positive sample to the synthesis process. (2) Positive Sample Synthesis: Generating synthetic positive samples by weighted aggregation of multiple positive samples; and (3) Negative Sample Augmentation: Inject the synthetic positive samples into randomly sampled negative samples with a coefficient $\alpha$ to control the proportion of positive sample information.}
    \label{fig:inject}
\end{figure}

% 与传统的启发式超边预测算法相比，基于学习的超边预测算法通过引入映射函数，将离散节点嵌入到连续的向量空间中，并利用向量距离来评估节点之间的相似性，从而预测节点之间是否能够形成超边。这一过程的核心在于构建一个高效的映射函数，该函数不仅需要确保在原始网络中“相似”的节点在向量空间中彼此接近，还需要确保“不相似”的节点在向量空间中彼此远离。为了实现这一目标，模型在训练过程中必须同时使用相似和不相似的信息。在超边预测任务中，通常假设已经形成超边或能够形成超边的节点之间是相似的，而无法形成超边的节点之间是不相似的。然而，在超图中，我们只能观测到已存在的超边集合$\mathcal{E}$，而无从得知哪些节点之间无法形成超边，因此也就无法获取构建高效映射函数所必需的不相似信息。幸运的是，真实超图非常稀疏，其实际存在的超边数量远远小于可能形成的超边数量。这意味着在未观察到的所有可能超边集合上进行随机负采样时，因为负样本的数量远远超过正样本，从而能够以很高的概率保证采样的负样本是真负样本（i.e., 负样本确实无法形成超边）。然而，如图\ref{fig:embedding_visual}所示，随机采样的负样本大多是易于区分的简单负样本，它们带给模型训练的价值是较小的。尽管存在一些启发式的负采样方法，例如通过合并多条超边或替换超边中的某个节点来生成难以区分的负样本，但这些方法无法保证负样本的真实性，可能会生成假负样本（i.e., 负样本实际上构成了超边或应该构成超边，只是尚未被观察到）。此外，由于不同场景下超边的形成机制不同，这些启发式方法并不具有普适性。
Compared to traditional heuristic hyperedge prediction algorithms, learning-based hyperedge prediction algorithms introduce a mapping function that embeds discrete nodes into a continuous vector space, allows the assessment of node similarity through vector distances. The core of this process lies in constructing an efficient mapping function that ensures similar nodes in the original network are close to each other in the vector space, while dissimilar nodes are far apart. To achieve this goal, the model must use both similar and dissimilar information during training. In hyperedge prediction tasks, it is typically assumed that nodes that have already formed or can form hyperedges are similar, while nodes that cannot form hyperedges are dissimilar. However, in a hypergraph, we can only observe the existing set of hyperedges $\mathcal{E}$, and we do not know which nodes cannot form hyperedges, making it impossible to obtain the necessary dissimilar information for building an efficient mapping function. Fortunately, real-world hypergraphs are extremely sparse, with the number of existent but unobserved hyperedges being far fewer than the possible hyperedges. Therefore, random negative sampling over all possible samples ensures a high probability that sampled negative samples are true negatives (\textit{i.e.}, they indeed cannot form hyperedges). However, as shown in Figure \ref{fig:embedding_visual}, randomly sampled negative samples are mostly easily distinguishable simple negatives, providing limited value for model training. Although some heuristic negative sampling methods exist, such as generating difficult-to-distinguish negative samples by merging multiple hyperedges or replacing one node within a hyperedge, these methods may generate false negatives (\textit{i.e.}, negative samples that actually constitute or should constitute hyperedges but have not been observed yet). Additionally, due to the different mechanisms of hyperedge formation across various scenarios, these heuristic methods lack generalizability.


% 针对负采样中存在的样本真实性与样本难度之间的矛盾，本文提出了一种新的超边负采样方法——基于正样本注入的难负采样方法HNS。该方法通过将正样本的表征注入到简单负样本的表征中，来提升负样本的难度。如图\ref{fig:inject}所示，HNS方法的核心在于在超边表征上进行正样本注入，具体包括三个关键步骤：正样本的选择、正样本的合成以及难负样本的生成。
To address the trade-off between authenticity and difficulty in negative sampling, the HNS method enhances the difficulty of negative samples by injecting the representations of positive samples into those of simple negative samples. As show in Figure \ref{fig:inject}, the core of the HNS method lies in performing positive sample injection on hyperedge representations, involving three key steps: Positive sample selection, positive sample synthesis, and hard negative sample generation.


% 在将正样本注入到负样本之前，首先需要解决正负样本的匹配问题。即对于给定的简单负样本，如何选择合适的正样本进行注入。在超边的嵌入空间中，不同正样本相对于某个负样本的位置决定了它们之间的相似度，进而影响生成的负样本的难度。HNS采用了一种动态选择策略，针对每个负样本，考虑所有正样本的影响，并根据正样本与负样本的相似性赋予不同的权重。具体而言，与负样本更接近的正样本会被赋予更高的权重。这一策略的设计基于以下两点考虑。一是相似度更高的正样本通常更接近分类决策边界。超边预测的分类器旨在学习正样本和负样本之间的分类边界，而与负样本更接近的正样本通常位于决策边界附近。这类样本在训练过程中能够更有效地帮助模型学习区分正负样本的能力，因此在注入时应赋予更高的权重。二是避免生成假负样本。距离负样本较远的正样本通常在特征空间中与负样本差异较大。如果在注入过程中给予此类正样本较高的权重，可能会导致其信息在训练过程中占据主导地位，从而削弱甚至覆盖原负样本的特征，容易生成假负样本，进而误导分类器，影响模型的判别能力。
Before injecting positive samples into negative samples, it is crucial to address the matching problem between positive and negative samples. Specifically, for a given simple negative sample, we need to determine which positive samples are suitable for injection. In the hyperedges embedding space, the positions of different positive samples relative to a particular negative sample determine their similarity, which in turn affects the difficulty of the generated negative samples. HNS employs a weighted selection strategy that considers influences of all positive samples for each negative by assigning different weights based on their distances (\textit{i.e.}, similarities to the target negative samples). Specifically, positive samples closer to the negative sample are assigned higher weights. This strategy is designed based on two considerations: Firstly, positive samples with shorter distances to the negative sample are typically closer to the classification decision boundary. The hyperedge prediction classifier aims to learn the boundary between positive and negative samples, and those positive samples near the negative sample are often located around this decision boundary. These samples are more valuable during model training, hence they should be given higher weights during injection. Secondly, positive samples that are farther from the negative sample generally exhibit greater differences in feature space. If such distant positive samples are given high weights during injection, their information may dominate the training process, potentially overshadowing or even replacing the features of the original negative sample. This could lead to the generation of false negative samples, misleading the classifier and degrading its discriminability.



% 为了量化正样本相对于负样本的权重，HNS采用了Scaled Dot-Product Attention \cite{vaswani2017attention}。具体而言，正样本$\mathbf{e}_j$对于某个负样本$\hat{\mathbf{e}}_i$的权重$s_{ij}$通过以下公式计算：
% \begin{equation}
% 	s_{ij} = \operatorname{softmax} \left(\frac{\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{j}^T}{\sqrt{h}} \right) 
% = \frac{ \exp \left( \left( \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{j}^{T} \right) / \sqrt{h} \right) }{ \sum_{l=1}^{n} \exp \left( \left( \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{l}^{T} \right) / \sqrt{h} \right) }
% \end{equation}
% 其中，$\frac{1}{\sqrt{h}}$用于防止梯度爆炸或梯度消失，确保训练过程的稳定性，而$\operatorname{softmax}$函数则用于将打分进行归一化。值得注意的是，$s_{ij}$的计算与模型的训练过程同步进行，即$s_{ij}$会随着模型的优化而动态调整。
To quantify the weights of positive samples relative to negative samples, HNS employs Scaled Dot-Product Attention \cite{vaswani2017attention}. Specifically, the weight $s_{ij}$ of a positive sample $\mathbf{e}_j$ for a given negative sample $\hat{\mathbf{e}}_i$ is calculated using the following formula:
\begin{equation}
	s_{ij} = \operatorname{softmax} \left(\frac{\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{j}^T}{\sqrt{h}} \right) 
= \frac{ \exp \left( \left( \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{j}^{T} \right) / \sqrt{h} \right) }{ \sum_{l=1}^{n} \exp \left( \left( \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} \cdot \mathbf{e}_{l}^{T} \right) / \sqrt{h} \right) }.
\end{equation}
Here, $1/\sqrt{h}$ is used to prevent gradient explosion or vanishing gradients, ensuring the stability during training. The $\operatorname{softmax}$ function \cite{bridle1990} normalizes the scores. Notably, the calculation of $s_{ij}$ is synchronized with the model's training process, meaning that $s_{ij}$ will be dynamically adjusted in the optimizing process of the model.


% 在计算得到不同正样本$\mathbf{e}_{j}$相对于负样本$\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i}$的权重$s_{ij}$后，HNS通过线性加权，得到一个对应于$\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i}$的合成正样本${\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$，即：
% \begin{equation}
% 	\mathbf{e}'_{i} = \sum_{j=1}^{N} s_{ij} \mathbf{e}_{j}
% \end{equation}
% 接下来，HNS采用凸组合的方式将合成正样本$\mathbf{e}'_{i}$注入到简单负样本$\hat{\mathbf{e}_i}$中，生成难负样本$\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$：
% \begin{equation}
% 	\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i} = (1 - \alpha) \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} + \alpha \mathbf{e}'_{i}
% \end{equation}
% 其中，$\alpha \in (0, 1)$是一个超参数，用于控制正样本信息在合成难负样本中的占比。通过调整注入强度$\alpha$，可以精确控制生成负样本的难度：$\alpha$的取值越大，生成的负样本越难以区分。特别地，当$\alpha=0$时，$\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i} = \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i}$，表示不进行注入，直接使用简单负样本作为最终的负样本，HNS方法退化为随机采样方法。$\alpha$的最优值取决于不同的超图数据集和超边预测算法，可通过实验进行确定。
After computing the weights $s_{ij}$ of different positive samples $\mathbf{e}_{j}$ relative to a negative sample $\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i}$, HNS synthesizes a corresponding positive sample ${\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$ for $\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i}$ using linear weighting, as:
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf{e}'_{i} = \sum_{j=1}^{N} s_{ij} \mathbf{e}_{j}.
\end{equation}
Next, HNS employs a convex combination to inject the synthesized positive sample $\mathbf{e}'_{i}$ into the simple negative sample $\hat{\mathbf{e}_i}$, generating a hard negative sample $\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$:
\begin{equation}
	\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i} = (1 - \alpha) \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{i} + \alpha \mathbf{e}'_{i},
\end{equation}
where $\alpha \in (0, 1)$ controls the proportion of positive sample information in the synthesized hard negative sample. By adjusting the injection strength $\alpha$, one can precisely control the difficulty of the generated negative sample: The larger of $\alpha$, the harder it is to distinguish the generated negative sample. Specifically, $\alpha=0$ corresponds to no injection, and then the simple negative sample is used directly as the final negative sample. In this case, the HNS method degenerates into a random sampling method. The optimal value of $\alpha$ depends on different hypergraph datasets and hyperedge prediction algorithms, which can be determined experimentally.



\subsection{Training and Prediction}
% HNS生成的难负样本$\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$与原始正样本$\mathbf{e}_j$共同构成训练集$\mathcal{E}'$，输入至基于多层感知机（MLP）的分类器进行端到端训练，联合优化编码器和分类器的参数。具体地，对于候选超边$e_q$（对应的嵌入表示为$\mathbf{e}_q$），模型预测其存在概率为：
% \begin{equation}
% 	\hat{y}_{q} = \sigma \left( \mathbf{W}^{(2)} \cdot \text{ReLU} \left( \mathbf{W}^{(1)} \mathbf{e}_q + \mathbf{b}^{(1)} \right) + \mathbf{b}^{(2)} \right)
% \end{equation}
% 其中：$\mathbf{W}^{(1)} \in \mathbb{R}^{h\times d}$, $\mathbf{W}^{(2)} \in \mathbb{R}^{1\times h}$为可学习权重矩阵；$\mathbf{b}^{(1)}$, $\mathbf{b}^{(2)}$为偏置项；$\text{ReLU}(\cdot)$激活函数引入非线性建模能力；$\sigma(\cdot)$为Sigmoid函数，将logit值映射为$[0,1]$的概率值。
The hard negative samples $\hat{\mathbf{e}}'_{i}$ generated by HNS, along with the original positive samples $\mathbf{e}_j$, form the training set $\mathcal{E}^{T}$, which is then fed into a multilayer perceptron (MLP)-based classifier \cite{bishop1995} for end-to-end training. This process jointly optimizes the parameters of both the encoder and the classifier. Specifically, for a candidate hyperedge $e_q$ (with its embedding representation denoted as $\mathbf{e}_q$), the model predicts its existence probability as:
\begin{equation}
	\hat{y}_{q} = \sigma \left( \mathbf{W}^{(2)} \cdot \text{ReLU} \left( \mathbf{W}^{(1)} \mathbf{e}_q + \mathbf{b}^{(1)} \right) + \mathbf{b}^{(2)} \right),
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{W}^{(1)} \in \mathbb{R}^{h\times d}$ and $\mathbf{W}^{(2)} \in \mathbb{R}^{1\times h}$ are learnable weight matrices; $\mathbf{b}^{(1)}$ and $\mathbf{b}^{(2)}$ are bias terms; $\text{ReLU}(\cdot)$ is the activation function that introduces non-linearity to the model, and $\sigma(\cdot)$ is the Sigmoid function, which maps the logit values to probability values in the range $[0,1]$.


% 为增强模型鲁棒性，我们在损失函数中引入L2权重衰减项以防止过拟合。模型的优化目标定义为加权二元交叉熵损失：
% \begin{equation}
% 	\mathcal{L}_{\text{pred}} = -\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}'|} \sum_{q \in \mathcal{E}'} \left[  y_q \log \hat{y}_q + (1-y_q) \log(1-\hat{y}_q) \right] + \lambda \|\Theta\|_2^2
% \end{equation}
% 其中, $y_{q} \in \{0, 1\}$是超边$e_q$的真实标签, $\hat{y}_{q}$则是模型对超边$q$的预测概率, $\lambda$为正则化强度，$\Theta$是所有的可学习参数. 该损失函数通过最大化正样本的预测得分和最小化负样本的预测得分, 来提高模型的判别能力. 在模型的训练过程中, 采用反向传播算法不断调整编码器和分类器的参数, 以最小化损失函数$L_{\text{pred}}$. 
To enhance the model's robustness, we introduce an $L_2$ term into the loss function to prevent overfitting. The optimization objective of the model is defined as a weighted binary cross-entropy loss:
\begin{equation}
	\mathcal{L}_{\text{pred}} = -\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}^{T}|} \sum_{q \in \mathcal{E}'} \left[  y_q \log \hat{y}_q + (1-y_q) \log(1-\hat{y}_q) \right] + \lambda \|\Theta\|_2^2,
\end{equation}
where $y_{q} \in \{0, 1\}$ is the true label of hyperedge $e_q$, $\hat{y}_{q}$ is the predicted probability for hyperedge $e_q$, $\lambda$ is the regularization strength, and $\Theta$ represents all learnable parameters. This loss function aims to maximize the prediction scores for positive samples and minimize the predicted scores for negative samples, thereby improving the model's discriminability. During the training process, the backpropagation algorithm \cite{rojas1996} is used to continuously adjust parameters of both the encoder and the classifier to minimize the loss function $\mathcal{L}_{\text{pred}}$.



\subsection{Algorithm Complexity}
% 在生成更具挑战性的负样本时, HNS方法并未引入额外的模型参数, 因此其空间复杂度与原始模型保持一致. 尽管计算过程中会产生一些中间结果, 但这些中间结果仅在计算时短暂占用内存, 不会被长期保存. 相比于模型自身的参数量, 这部分中间结果对空间复杂度的影响可以忽略不计. 
When generating more challenging negative samples, the HNS method does not introduce additional model parameters, thus maintaining the same space complexity as the original model. Although some intermediate results are generated during the computation, they only temporarily occupy memory during calculation and are not stored long-term. Compared to the number of parameters in the model itself, the impact of these intermediate results on space complexity is negligible.


% 在时间复杂度方面, HNS方法主要的额外开销来自于正负样本对之间的权重$s_{ij}$的计算. 具体来说, 对于每个合成的难负样本, 模型需要计算其与所有正样本之间的相似度. 这一过程的时间复杂度为$O(m_1 \times m_2 \times h)$, 其中$m_1$表示正样本的数量, $m_2$表示每个正样本生成的难负样本数量, $h$为超边嵌入表示的维度. 由于需要对每一对正负样本进行相似度计算, 在大型超图数据集上, 这种计算可能会变得较为耗时. 为了减少计算量并避免模型陷入局部极小值点, 神经网络通常采用批次(batch)方式进行训练. 具体而言, 在每次迭代中, 模型仅处理一个较小的批次样本, 而不是整个数据集\cite{krizhevsky2017imagenet}. 因此, 时间复杂度中的$m_1$和$m_2$实际上是批次内的正样本和难负样本数量, 它们远小于整个数据集的样本数目. 这种批次处理方式使得HNS方法即使面对大规模数据集也能保持高效的性能. 此外, 相似度计算可以通过矩阵运算实现, 并充分利用GPU加速, 从而进一步提升计算效率, 确保HNS方法在实际应用中的高效性和可扩展性.
In terms of time complexity, the primary additional overhead of the HNS comes from the computation of weights $s_{ij}$ between positive and negative sample pairs. Specifically, for each generated simple negative sample, the model needs to compute its similarity with all positive samples. The time complexity of this process is $O(m_1 \times m_2 \times h)$, where $m_1$ represents the number of positive samples, $m_2$ represents the number of simple negative samples, and $h$ is the dimensionality of the hyperedge embedding representation. Since similarity calculations are required for every pair of positive and negative samples, this computation can become quite time-consuming on large hypergraph datasets. To reduce computational load and avoid the model getting stuck in local minima, neural networks typically employ batch training. Specifically, in each iteration, the model processes only a small batch of samples rather than the entire dataset \cite{krizhevsky2017imagenet}. Therefore, in the time complexity expression, $m_1$ and $m_2$ actually refer to the numbers of positive and negative samples within a batch, which are much smaller than the total number of samples in the entire dataset. This batch processing approach allows the HNS to maintain high performance even on large-scale datasets. Additionally, similarity computations can be implemented using matrix operations and can take full advantage of GPU acceleration, further reducing computational cost. This ensures that the HNS remains highly efficient and scalable in practical applications.


