\subsection{Appendix F: proof of the Proposition \ref{asydenprop}}
 As suggested we rescale $z=\sqrt{N} w, \quad a=\sqrt{N} \alpha$ and keep the parameters $w,\alpha$ fixed as $N\to \infty$.
Note that the rescaling implies $\delta=N\Delta, \, \Delta=|\alpha|^2-(\alpha\overline{w}+\overline{\alpha}w)$. Applying the Laplace method one finds the following
leading asymptotic large-$N$ behaviour of the functions $ I^{(k)}(N,N\Delta)$ defined in Eq.(\ref{delta}) for a fixed integer $k$:
\begin{equation}\label{asyI}
 I^{(k)}(N,N\Delta)\sim \frac{1}{N(1+\Delta)} \,\, \mbox{for} \, \Delta>-1 \quad \mbox{and}\quad   I^{(k)}(N,N\Delta)\sim \sqrt{\frac{2\pi}{N}}
 \frac{e^{-N(1+\Delta)}}{|\Delta|^{N+k-1}}\,\, \mbox{for} \, \Delta<-1.
\end{equation}
This should be combined with the asymptotics of the incomplete $\Gamma-$function for a fixed integer $l$:
  \begin{equation}\label{asyGamma}
\frac{\Gamma(N-l,N|w|^2)}{\Gamma(N)} \sim \frac{1}{N^{l}} \,\, \mbox{for} \, |w|^2<1\quad \mbox{and}\quad \frac{\Gamma(N-l,N|w|^2)}{\Gamma(N)}\sim
\frac{e^{N(1-|w|^2)}}{N^l\sqrt{2\pi N}}
 \frac{|w|^{2(N-l)}}{|w|^2-1} \,\, \mbox{for} \, |w|^2>1.
\end{equation}
 Writing $w=|w|e^{i\theta}$ and $\alpha=|\alpha|e^{i\theta_{\alpha}}$ one easily finds that the condition
$\Delta>-1$ is equivalent to $|w|\cos{(\theta-\theta_{\alpha})}<\frac{1}{2}\left(|\alpha|+|\alpha|^{-1}\right)$ and hence is always satisfied
in the interior of the unit circle: $|w|<1$ for any $\alpha$. Applying the corresponding asymptotics one then easily arrives to the statement of
 Eq.(\ref{inside}). At the same time outside the unit circle for $|w|>1$
assuming simultaneously  $\Delta<-1$ one arrives to the statement Eq.(\ref{asydenout}).

