Looking for strictly positive steady states (`coexistence steady states'), we can assume $v_0 \neq 0$. 
Dividing the steady state form of \eqref{v_hom_eq} by $v_0$ and solving for $u_0$ we find,
\begin{equation}
 u_0 = (\gamma_v + v_0)(1-v_0). \label{uss}  
\end{equation}
Solving the steady state version of \eqref{w_hom_eq} for $w_0$ and substituting in the expression \eqref{uss}, we find,
\begin{equation}
w_0 = \frac{\sigma _{w}+\frac{\rho _{w}u_0v_0}{\gamma _{w}+v_0}}{\mu _{w}} = \frac{\sigma _{w}+\frac{\rho _{w}v_0\left(\gamma _{v}+v_0\right)\left(1-v_0\right)}{\gamma _{w}+v_0}}{\mu _{w}}.    \label{wss}
\end{equation}

