 \caption{\justifying Phase diagram of the model in random regular graphs with $g=c=5$. The figure includes BP's predictions (solid lines), the results of Monte Carlo simulations (squares and triangles), and our analytic computation of the stability of the paramagnetic solution (dashed lines). Different colors represent BP's predictions for different initial conditions obtained using a binomial distribution (see Eq. \ref{eq:init_binomial}) to assign the initial value of the messages. Monte Carlo simulations are performed over systems with $N=10^{4}$ individuals. When $p=0.5$, the initial state has zero magnetization (no alignment of the opinions). When $p=1.0$, the initial state is completely aligned ($m=1$). BP's transition lines have an uncertainty of order $d\alpha=0.001$, not shown since it is of the size of the lines themselves. The inserted graphic shows the two branches of BP's free energy density for different $\alpha$ at $T = 0.35$. The blue triangles are obtained with completely aligned initial conditions, and the red squares with random initial conditions.} 
